From: ProjectM TV contributors
Subject: [PATCH] Preserve evaluator finite guards under Clang and GNU fast-math

Append -fno-finite-math-only only to TreeFunctions.c after the evaluator's
existing fast-math options. Keep reassociation, reciprocal transforms,
contraction, approximate function permissions and every other source's flags.
Place the policy in vendored evaluator CMake so engine and host consumers
share it, rather than relying on Android application's build configuration.

This restores existing pow/pow_op and invsqrt NaN-to-zero guards on Android
in addition to protecting the proposed small-finite/remainder repairs.
That additional invalid-input behavior requires explicit disposition.
MSVC fast-math policy remains unqualified; no /fp policy is changed here.

---
--- a/vendor/projectm-eval/projectm-eval/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/vendor/projectm-eval/projectm-eval/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -79,6 +79,12 @@
     PRJM_F_SIZE=${PROJECTM_EVAL_FLOAT_SIZE}
 )
 
+# Keep explicit NaN/Inf guards in TreeFunctions.c under evaluator fast-math.
+# Source options follow directory/target options, overriding finite-only assumptions.
+if(CMAKE_C_COMPILER_ID MATCHES "^(Clang|AppleClang|GNU)$")
+    set_property(SOURCE TreeFunctions.c APPEND PROPERTY COMPILE_OPTIONS -fno-finite-math-only)
+endif()
+
 set_target_properties(projectM_eval PROPERTIES
                       EXPORT_NAME Eval
                       )
